        "That parallel door has its own competition and its own paperwork, and it varies by university and even by faculty, so a family should confirm the current year's specific requirements directly with each target university's admissions office well before application season rather than relying on general online guidance, which changes as policy shifts. A completed IB Diploma is generally viewed favourably within these tracks, and a strong HL combination in a student's intended field — HL Mathematics for engineering, HL Sciences for a health-related degree — carries real weight in the file review most of these special tracks use instead of a single test score.",
        "Overseas recognition is, for many IB families in Korea, the larger draw than the domestic route. The IB Diploma and Cambridge A Level are both widely and consistently recognised by universities across the US, UK, Canada, Australia and continental Europe, generally more portably internationally than the Suneung itself, which is little known outside Korea. Many US universities award course credit or advanced standing for HL scores of 5 and above, though the exact policy is set institution by institution and worth checking directly on each target university's own published credit page before finalising HL subject choices in Grade 11.",
        "Predicted grades matter earlier than final results for any overseas application, since UK and US applications go in during the first half of DP2, well before May exams. That makes the fall of the second DP year the highest-leverage tutoring window for students applying abroad — the moment to firm up the one or two Higher Level subjects where a teacher's current prediction sits below what a stronger mock result could support, since predictions are what admissions officers actually see on results day for most applications.",
        "None of this recognition removes the practical need to plan early. A family should decide, ideally before Grade 10 subject choices lock in, whether the target is a Korean university's special-admission track, an overseas university, or both, since HL subject combinations that serve one path well do not automatically serve the other equally. We build tutoring priorities around whichever specific universities and programmes a family names, rather than a generic assumption about what \"looks good.\"",
